####################################################################
# cat2a_priority_aggregate.dlog — SHADOW, EXPERIMENTAL. NOT WIRED INTO
# THE PRODUCTION PATH (engine/replay_driver.py's build_script does not
# import this file; nothing in the live pipeline depends on it).
#
# Rewrite of cat2a_process_priority.dlog's expensive 14-atom self-join
# ("does an active alarm with rank >= mine exist for the same process")
# as a standing, incrementally-maintained AGGREGATE instead. Confirmed
# empirically (this session's spike work) that RDFox maintains a standing
# MAX aggregate's value in genuinely constant time per insert/retract,
# flat from group sizes of 10 up to 1500, including with graph-scoped
# members retracted via whole-graph DELETE WHERE (the real production
# eviction mechanism) — not just theoretically "more RSP-aligned," but
# empirically verified not to reintroduce the same concurrency-scaling
# cost the self-join has.
#
# GROUP KEY: composite (patient, process), NOT process alone —
# mda:isPropertyOf's pivot (?process) is a STANDING, patient-independent
# CONCEPT node (e.g. physiologicalProcess:CardiacContraction), so grouping
# by ?process alone would silently aggregate ACROSS different patients the
# instant they share one dstore — the exact cross-patient leak bug already
# found and fixed once in the self-join version (see
# cat2a_process_priority.dlog's own "SAME-PATIENT CONSTRAINT" comment).
# SKOLEM is NOT usable inside AGGREGATE's BIND (confirmed empirically:
# "Builtin function with name 'SKOLEM' does not exist" in this context) —
# CONCAT+IRI mints the composite key instead, confirmed correct.
#
# ORDERING REQUIREMENT THIS RULE IMPOSES ON ITS CALLER (see
# engine/shadow_incremental.py): mda:shadowMaxActiveRank for a
# (patient,process) key reflects EVERY alarm whose full chain — INCLUDING
# hasPriority/priorityRank — is currently present. An arriving alarm's own
# rank would trivially satisfy MAX(?activeRank) >= itself the instant it's
# inserted, so the caller MUST query this aggregate BEFORE inserting the
# arriving alarm's own hasPriority triple (a two-phase insert — chain data
# first, priority triple held back until after the check) to correctly
# answer "did some OTHER, already-active alarm already qualify" rather
# than "do I qualify against myself."
####################################################################

@prefix mda:      <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix alarmcat:  <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/alarm-category/> .

## FIX (this session, confirmed against real patient 2826): independent
## per-hop graph variables (?g8..?g14) let RDFox mix-and-match across
## every currently-open alarm's own redundant copy of the same structural
## facts, since hasSensor/sensorProducesSignal/analyzedBy get re-minted
## into EVERY currently-active alarm's own persistent graph (kb.node_kind:
## Device/Sensor/Signal "individuated", SignalAnalysis untagged — both
## route to ground_chain's `background`) and hasMessage/triggeredBy/
## producesMetric/approximates/hasPriority always co-locate in that same
## alarm's own transient graph (Metric is "stateful" -> `condition`;
## insert_alarm bundles msg_graph+cond_graph into one tgraph block). A
## direct CSV dump of one alarm's own (non-cross-alarm) chain lookup
## under the old ?g8..?g14 shape returned 24,435 redundant rows for what
## is structurally exactly 1 fact — confirmed the independent-variable
## shape, not group size, was the multiplier. ?gCond groups everything
## that lives in one alarm's transient graph; ?gStruct groups everything
## that lives in that same alarm's persistent graph.
[?ppKey, mda:shadowMaxActiveRank, ?maxRank] :-
    AGGREGATE(
        [?active, mda:hasCategory, alarmcat:Physiological] ?gCond,
        [?active, mda:hasMessage, ?activeMsg] ?gCond,
        [?activeMsg, mda:concernsPatient, ?patient] ?gCond,
        [?activeMsg, mda:triggeredBy, ?activeDevice] ?gCond,
        [?activeDevice, mda:hasSensor, ?activeSensor] ?gStruct,
        [?activeSensor, mda:sensorProducesSignal, ?activeSignal] ?gStruct,
        [?activeSignal, mda:analyzedBy, ?activeAnalysis] ?gStruct,
        [?activeAnalysis, mda:producesMetric, ?activeMetric] ?gCond,
        [?activeMetric, mda:approximates, ?activeProperty] ?gCond,
        [?activeProperty, mda:isPropertyOf, ?process],
        [?active, mda:hasPriority, ?activePrio] ?gCond,
        [?activePrio, mda:priorityRank, ?activeRank],
        BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(?patient), "|", STR(?process))) AS ?ppKey)
        ON ?ppKey
        BIND MAX(?activeRank) AS ?maxRank
    ) .

# VALIDATION — see engine/shadow_incremental.py's own harness for the
# equivalence check against cat2a_pos/cat2a_neg and the composite-key
# cross-patient isolation check; not yet run against real RDFox as part of
# a validated regression at the time this file was written (that's the
# whole point of the shadow harness — verify before promoting).
